\begin_layout Section
Defining an Analysis Method
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To make this discussion concrete we will look at the implementation of the
 FBAT analysis method.
 First, we need to choose two file names for the analysis method: one for
 the C++ code and one for the class definition.
 We will use the files 
\series bold
write_fbat.cpp
\series default
 and 
\series bold
write_fbat_ext.h, 
\series default
respectively.
 (Technically, there can be executable code in the class definition.)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Class definition
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
We define a new class and derive it from the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset


\series bold
CLASS_ANALYSIS
\series default

\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 base class.
 (I like to put the string 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

CLASS_
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 at the start of the class name.) After defining the constructor/destructor
 there are a lot of standard methods that can be defined and other methods
 that will be forward referenced and defined in the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

code
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 file.
 And of course you can define any methods you need to define the semantics
 of the analysis.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
All these standard methods must be a subset of what is defined in 
\series bold
CLASS_ANALYSIS
\series default
 (see file 
\series bold
\emph on
analysis.h
\series default
\emph default
).
 In particular, a few dozen virtual methods are defined that contain only
 a 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

return false
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 statement.
 There are extensive comments in the 
\series bold
\emph on
analysis.
\series default
\emph default
h
\emph on
 
\emph default
file that document what these switches do.
 These virtual methods turn off or on features of the Mega2 system necessary
 for this particular analysis method being defined.
 The base class defines these switches to be off.
 Thus if that is the correct state for the new analysis, it is not necessary
 to repeat the method definition since it will be inherit from the base
 class.
 Of course, the method is virtual so you may define it to 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

return true
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 for this analysis.
 Obviously, in this case it would be necessary to copy the appropriate definitio
n into the new class definition.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Toward the end of the 
\series bold
CLASS_ANALYSIS
\series default
 definition, there are a few more virtual methods that you might want to
 override for your class: 
\emph on
ped_ind_defaults
\emph default
, 
\emph on
sub_prog_name
\emph default
, 
\emph on
sub_prog_name_to_sub_option
\emph default
, 
\emph on
and interactive_sub_prog_name_to_sub_option
\emph default
.
 Often, certainly for FBAT, you only need to define 
\emph on
ped_ind_defaults
\emph default
, which indicates how to print out the pedigree and person information.
 For the other functions, the default is fine.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Finally, the four methods: 
\emph on
create_output_file
\emph default
, 
\emph on
get_file_names
\emph default
, 
\emph on
file_names, 
\emph default
and 
\emph on
replace_chr_number
\emph default
 are declared with the class definition but defined in the code file.
 
\emph on
create_output_file
\emph default
 is responsible for doing data transformations and creating all the output
 files needed by the analysis program.
 The other methods support the idiosyncratic way that Mega2 generates file
 names (with embedded chromosomes and suffix that indicates file type).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Class code
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The header of the file is standard boiler plate and you should just copy
 it from an existing .cpp, such as 
\series bold
write_fbat.cpp
\series default
.
 You will of course not include the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

write_fbat_ext.h
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 (and 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

fbat.R.h
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

) header, but use the header file for your class.
 I like to follow the header by the code to generate each of the types of
 files needed by the analysis and at the end of the file I define the 
\emph on
create_output_file
\emph default
 to call all the methods (or functions) defined earlier in the file.
 Finally, at the end of the file there is the code to interactively query
 the user for the names to be used for each type of file, 
\emph on
get_file_names
\emph default
.
 And there is the code to glue the names together and to allow components
 (like the chromosome number) to be changed as necessary.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
So lets look deeper into how an output file is generated.
 But first we need to make a few adjustments to the Mega2 files so these
 new files are compiled and available.
\end_layout

