\begin_layout Subsubsection
class file_ops [in file_ops.h]
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

file_ops
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 opens [
\emph on
filep_open
\emph default
()] and closes [
\emph on
filep_close
\emph default
()] files as well as prints [
\emph on
pr_printf
\emph default
(), 
\emph on
pr_puts
\emph default
(), and 
\emph on
pr_nl
\emph default
()] to files.
 If the file name ends in 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

.gz
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

, the compression library, zlib, will be used to write the file data.
 The print methods use the file descriptor member of the object and take
 the same arguments as printf and fputs, respectively.
 The 
\emph on
filep_open
\emph default
 method calls the virtual function, 
\emph on
file_header
\emph default
, after the file is opened; while the method 
\emph on
filep_close
\emph default
() calls the virtual function, 
\emph on
file_trailer
\emph default
, before the file is closed and the virtual function, 
\emph on
file_post
\emph default
, after it is closed.
 These virtual functions allow derived classes to easily supply headers
 and trailer data for the file.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In addition, there are additional methods to flush the data to disk, 
\emph on
file_flush
\emph default
, and delete the named file, 
\emph on
filep_delete
\emph default
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Note: The object destructor calls the 
\emph on
filep_close
\emph default
 method; so it is never necessary to explicitly call 
\emph on
filep_close
\emph default
.
\end_layout

