\begin_layout Subsection
Output Loop Classes
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The loop classes are defined in the files: 
\series bold
loop.h 
\series default
and 
\series bold
loop.cpp
\series default
.
 These supply an Inner loop and Outer loop.
 Both loops contain several different classes each of which iterates through
 people, chromosomes and markers in a designated order.
 Creating an output file for Mega2 is achieved by creating a new class that
 is derived from a chosen Output loop class and a chosen Inner loop class.
 It is easiest to explain the Inner loop and then the Outer loop but programmati
cally you need to setup the Outer loop and then the Inner loop.
 So it might be best to read this section twice.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Note: (This will also make more sense on a second reading.) Both the Inner
 and Outer loop are derived from 
\series bold
person_locus_entry
\series default
 class.
 When we create the output file class, it will be derived from both an outer
 class and an inner class.
 This is called multiple inheritance.
 And each of these classes is derived from the person_locus_entry class.
 This is called OOPS.
 Although this could lead us into a long discussion about inheritance, the
 basic question is do we want the inner loop object to inherit from a different
 object than the outer loop object.
 This would be the C++ default.
 But we want both objects to inherit from the same person_locus_entry object
 and share data.
 To have this happen correctly, the definition of each type of loop class
