\begin_layout Subsubsection
Outer loop
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Mega2 sometimes outputs one file of data.
 But it can also output separate files in new directory for each different
 trait and having a different name (suffix) for different chromosomes.
 The example shown above processes one chromosome.
 (Although if the _numchr value is -1, it will process all chromosomes into
 one output file.) How do we iterate through all the chromosomes (and/or
 possibly traits)? This is what the Outer loop classes support.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Thus building on the example above, supposed we want to iterate on chromosomes.
 The Outer loop class, 
\series bold
\emph on
chr
\series default
\emph default
, handles this case.
 There is only one 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

real
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 method, 
\emph on
iterate
\emph default
(), in the class, but quite a few virtual function that are stubbed out
 as empty to be replaced in a derived class as necessary.
 (All this is analogous to the Inner loop class described above.) The goal
 of this class is to define the file that will be used by the Inner loop
 and then iterate over all the chromosomes.
 Or if chosen by the user, not iterate at all and process all the chromosomes
 together.
 Line 22 starts a loop; but if _chrom_loop is zero, the loop will be degenerate,
 and only go through one cycle and abort at line 43.
 The code in lines 24-35 assure that the correct chromosomes for will be
 iterated through.
 If _chrom_loop is set choose the correct chromosome (line 25) for each
 cycle; otherwise choose all the chromosomes (line 29) or the only single
 chromosome (line 32).
 The interesting part of this loop construct is lines 37/42 which invoke
 the virtual methods 
\emph on
chr_start/chr_end
\emph default
.
 These are intended to be be overwritten as necessary similar to the start/end
 virtual methods defined earlier.
 Finally, line 39, 
\emph on
make_file
\emph default
(), is the glue that will connect the Outer loop to the Inner loop.
 In particular, the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

new
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 class discussed earlier must define a 
\emph on
make_file
\emph default
