\begin_layout Subsection
Microsoft Windows
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection*
Visual Studio
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
First, you should obtain a copy of the latest Visual Studio or Visual Studio
 Express from Microsoft 
\begin_inset Flex URL
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout

www.visualstudio.com
\end_layout

\end_inset

.
 If you are given a choice, only the C and C++ compilers tool chain is necessary.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Gmake
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
You will also need a copy of Gnu make
\begin_inset Flex URL
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout

http://www.gnu.org/software/make/
\end_layout

\end_inset

 for windows to run the make scripts that build Mega2.
 A windows binary can be found at 
\begin_inset Flex URL
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout

http://gnuwin32.sourceforge.net/packages/make.htm
\end_layout

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Path
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
You must put the compiler and make binaries on your path.
 The easiest way to put the compiler and tools onto your path is to 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

source
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

c:
\backslash
Program Files
\backslash
Microsoft
\backslash
Microsoft Visual Studio
\backslash
Common
\backslash
bin
\backslash
vs32vars.bat XXXXX
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

.
 A simple 
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
PATH %PATH%;<full path to make binary>
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
will put the make program in your path.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
NOTE: These two procedures have to be repeated every time you need to compile
 Mega2.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Execution
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
With these prerequisites fulfilled, you need to enter the 
\series bold
\emph on
Mega2/srcdir
\series default
\emph default
 directory and type
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
make
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
to compile Mega2.
 The binary that is produced is self contained and will run on any windows
 system.
\end_layout

